{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Outcome\nLanded as Gerrit change 1217 at merged commit `750a56b3b004f3c3f4cc1b456d3c56bd7809b87d`. `BindingStore.set_baseline` now filters the five mirrored fields, preserves keys whose value is `None`, returns early when the stored baseline is equal, and never reads the clock or writes `baseline_advanced_at`. This execution-state record supersedes planning-time line references while preserving the original rationale and acceptance contract.\n\n## Planning-time root cause and measured value\nBefore A1, `set_baseline` unconditionally replaced `entry[\"baseline\"]` and stamped `baseline_advanced_at = _now_iso()`. The stamp had no production reader. Across the original 40-revision study, baseline values changed 0 entries while the stamp changed 1,144 entries in a sort-ordered ~18 MB file, producing pathological git delta churn. The write-when-changed guard is byte-neutral for that historical corpus; the measured packed-cost win is from retiring the volatile stamp. Planning evidence lives in session log `1cb6-d553-6565-49b4`.\n\n## Implemented behavior and call sites\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py:451-466` owns filtering, equality comparison, early return, and changed-value assignment.\n- `BindingStore.seed_baselines_from_snapshot` begins at `binding_store.py:468` and delegates through the same guarded method.\n- `reconcile._advance_baselines` begins at `reconcile.py:520` and needs no caller edit because the guard is centralized.\n- The inbound-adopt dynamic call is at `apply_inbound_records.py:257-260` and receives the same centralized behavior.\n- Historical serialized stamp keys are inert; cleanup of cache history/current cache artifacts belongs to the parent epic rollout and rewrite, not to a new production reader or migration in A1.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state preserve byte-identical `bindings.json`. Proved by `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py::test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head`.\n- [x] The same integration test preserves the tracker HEAD, proving the unchanged second pass creates no commit. Run with `pytest tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py::test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head`.\n- [x] Exact identifier search finds no production reference: `grep -Rnw baseline_advanced_at src/rebar` returns no match.\n- [x] Every new baseline written by `set_baseline` omits `baseline_advanced_at`; unit tests fail fast if baseline writes read the clock. Proved in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_baseline.py`.\n- [x] A present-but-null baseline field round-trips as present. Proved by `test_present_null_baseline_field_round_trips`.\n- [x] A changed baseline persists the new value and changes serialized bytes, so the guard cannot degenerate into never-write. Proved by `test_changed_baseline_updates_serialized_bytes`.\n- [x] Repeated `seed_baselines_from_snapshot` input preserves serialized bytes, and the inbound-adopt path retains its existing focused coverage.\n- [x] The complete repository suite is green: `make test` passed with 8,519 passed, 39 skipped, and 175 deselected; `make lint` and `make typecheck` passed.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Marginal packed cost over the frozen 40-SHA corpus is at most 25% of baseline. Operator evidence on this ticket records the exact corpus, transformation, serializer, repack flags, pack byte counts, formula, and result: 13.84 KiB/version before versus 2.33 KiB/version after (16.8%).\n- [x] Gerrit change 1217 received `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`, then merged without unresolved comments.\n\n## Files\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — implementation.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` — read-only caller context.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py` — read-only dynamic caller context.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_baseline.py` — unit/serialization oracle.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py` — stateful-fake git-backed E2E oracle.\n\nScope: completed A1 only; standalone follow-up story `deeb-89c1-1080-4690` owns plan-review evidence-kind classification."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785699851707495001,"uuid":"4662d15b-2705-463e-818b-cd7e93c24802"}